Filetype: Flipper NFC device
Version: 4
Device type: Mifare Classic
# UID is exactly 4 bytes (Mifare Classic single-size). The chosen value
# 04 DE AD BE is arbitrary + safe -- no real card matches this.
# BCC (Block Check Character) is XOR(0x04, 0xDE, 0xAD, 0xBE) = 0xC9.
UID: 04 DE AD BE
ATQA: 04 44
SAK: 08
# Mifare Classic specific data
Mifare Classic type: 1K
Data format version: 1
# Mifare Classic blocks, '??' means unknown data

# ==============================================================
#  Mifare_Classic_1k_Template.nfc
#
#  Purpose: structural Mifare Classic 1K tag for emulation testing.
#  The UID here is *deliberately* 04:DE:AD:BE so it cannot
#  impersonate any real contactless card. Do NOT replace the UID
#  with a card you do not own -- you can lock yourself out of
#  door readers that perform whitelist matching.
#
#  ATQA + SAK match the real Mifare Classic 1K family
#  signatures, so the Flipper can enumerate this file as a
#  Mifare Classic card without complaint.
#
#  Layout notes (all 64 blocks present so the file loads and
#  emulates fully):
#    - Block 0  : manufacturer block. UID(4) + BCC(1) + SAK(1) +
#                 ATQA(2) + 8 manufacturer bytes = 16 bytes.
#    - Blocks 1-2, 4-6, ... : data blocks (all zeroes, erased
#                 card state).
#    - Blocks 3, 7, 11, ..., 63 : sector trailers. The factory
#                 default FF FF FF FF FF FF FF 07 80 69 FF FF FF
#                 FF FF FF means Key A = Key B = all-FF and the
#                 access bits allow any key to read/write.
#
#  If you ever fill these with real keys, treat them like
#  credentials.
# ==============================================================

Block 0: 04 DE AD BE C9 08 04 44 62 63 64 65 66 67 68 69
